<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dušan's Code</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1349">1349</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Zakonik</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dušan's Code was the law code of the Serbian Empire, adopted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a> at an assembly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skopje">Skopje</a> in 1349 and enlarged in 1354. It set out the rights of the Church, the nobility and the peasantry and drew on Byzantine law. It is one of the most important legal monuments of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dusans-code.jpg" alt="Dušan's Code" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vukašin of Serbia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Du%C5%A1an%27s_Code,_Prizren_manuscript,_15th_c.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
